discussion_comments.comment_body:
**[Suggestion]** Publisher `build` failure phase is untested end-to-end — Concrete cost: every test that sets `PREPARE_FAILURE_PHASE` uses `'install'`. The publisher's `case build)` arm that maps to `npm run build` is never rendered. A refactor breaking that arm (e.g. typo in the command name) would produce incorrect published text with no test catching it.

```suggestion
      const real = render(dir, {
        NAME: 'fail',
        VERDICT: 'fail',
        PREPARE_FAILURE_PHASE: 'install',
      });
      expect(real).toContain('treated as a PR failure');

      const buildFail = render(dir, {
        NAME: 'buildfail',
        VERDICT: 'fail',
        PREPARE_FAILURE_PHASE: 'build',
      });
      expect(buildFail).toContain('treated as a PR failure');
      expect(buildFail).toContain('`npm run build`');
```

_— qwen3.7-max via Qwen Code /review_

